These describe practice and acceptance criteria. They do not claim to have run actual art-model experiments, produced reference images, or verified execution in a live TW5 runtime.
<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/tests`>>
!! Proposed acceptance tests before promotion

* TW5 declarations remain untouched, and all invoked argument names match `art()` or the three optional existing Folio procedures.
* Every compact Inscription source invocation remains at or under 1,024 characters; every extended Folio block at or under 6,000 characters.
* References and external URLs remain outside transmitted image-facing blocks. Cross-links resolve to exact branch paths.
* The new examples remain divergent in worktype and do not create unwanted default materials, figures, labels, backgrounds or composition boards.
* The three transparency meanings and artistic/technical/reception records do not collapse together.
* Rights, actual alpha and exact strings are never asserted from apparent visual resemblance alone.
* A receiver may be unavailable; mark empirical test cases `unverified`, never claim they ran.
* Source and target branch heads, changed files, and any build/test limitations are reported with provenance.

The first wave is documentation and semantic test planning. Later empirical testing requires named receivers, controlled input conditions, appropriate source rights, and explicit operator direction.
<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/aftermath`>>
No automatic promotion to stable doctrine. Deferred extraction and repetition cleanup stay outside this branch's scope pending their own judgment. The prose remains open to scrutiny, especially whether any companion contract becomes an unwanted workflow requirement.
<<~/ahu>>

